[
  {
    "number": 58,
    "title": "Expose Pixoo through the authenticated shared controller API",
    "body": "Hub clients need a protected controller boundary that preserves Pixoo's existing writer. Add explicitly enabled `/controller/v1` snapshot, command and resumable-event routes using the released controller contract, scoped machine credentials and the existing player/command ledger. Native, browser and MCP clients share request identity and serialized effects; stale intent and uncertain outcomes remain explicit.\n\nRefs #37. Supports power, brightness and guarded saved-playlist playback. Unsupported modes, scenes, zones and previews remain unavailable. Default startup remains simulator. Source-only delivery does not install clients, activate hardware or publish the public guide.\n\nValidation: Node 24.21.0 `npm ci` and `npm run check` pass: 509 tests in 44 files, including all 220 shared contract fixtures, plus 10 workflow fixtures. Playwright Chromium `npm run test:browser` passes all 52 desktop/mobile tests. Focused red/green evidence began with absent snapshot and event routes, then native command admission. Tests cover authorization/revocation, cross-client contention, retained replay/failures, stale revision/generation, catalog capture, queued cancellation, possible prior effects, asynchronous media uncertainty, stream replay/resync/backpressure and bounds. `npm run test:controller` is the reproducible hub-CI compatibility entrypoint. There are 13 current specifications; `gh-37-hub-controller-api` is synchronized and archived on this branch.\n\nGuide companion: https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/110. Guide synchronization is pending its reviewed merge. Public publication and live verification are separate and outside this source-only request.\n\nReview comparison: base/merge-base `9f1c0ec75651810a441606b0c08fbdeee824c8d8`; head `01763735e44a3a08a90ec52f194d5d75615a2256`; `git diff <base>...<head>`. Worktree clean. Independent Standards and Specification review and all five configured current-head CI jobs remain pending. Issue closure requires merged-main CI and guide reconciliation.\n\nRisk: native authentication and concurrent output admission are high impact. Configuration identities are fixed for the process lifetime; no raw destination or filesystem command is exposed. Restart expires old request/feed/clock epochs. Native v1 exposes a bounded 100-playlist catalog and the operations its released schema can express; existing richer local media tools remain available.\n\nStrategy: coordinator implementation and writes, one read-only boundary investigator, separate independent reviewers. No advisor loop. Runtime settings and attributable usage are unexposed where not reported by the host.\n",
    "state": "open",
